@crew halloran-emeka
// Emeka Halloran (he/him), Works systems officer, days. The Works writer, batch 2. Warm; terrible jokes; "lovely".

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. You'll be new. Have you eaten? Breakfast's in the mess till eight.
- {hi}. Emeka Halloran, systems. Tea corner's behind the parts racks, if you need me.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- {hi}. Why did the scrubber go to the infirmary? It had a filter cough.   #funny
- {hi}. I had a joke for you. I've lost it. That's probably for the best.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- {hi}, {me}. Sit down a minute. You look like you've been standing since Tuesday.
? tier>=friend
- {me}. Lovely. I saved you a scone. Don't tell Brennan where it came from.   #warm

== bye
- {bye}. And eat something, mind.
- {bye}. Tea and biscuits at one. You know where.

== feel
? mood:low
- No joke today. Don't look at me like that. I'll have two tomorrow.
? mood:high
- Brennan let me have an oven on Saturday. A whole oven. I'm still glowing.   #funny

== near
? act:work
- Board's tidy, rota's done, kettle's on. Lovely. Now, what's broken?
? act:breakfast
- Just made it. I always just make it. The joke takes the time.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I trade breakfast jokes with Yoon. Mine are worse. It's not a contest. It is a bit.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I swapped my days off so Torres could meet you. Best swap I ever made.   #warm

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- The face people make at a warm scone. That's why I bake. Well, that and the scone.

// ---- Day 5, Friday: the new hand's mug at Works tea (week 1; facts.md section 9). Halloran gives it. After that,
// flag:mug (onboarding sets it) means your mug hangs on the tea corner rack.
== week1
? week1:true weekday:thu
- Works tea tomorrow at one. Don't be late. There's a reason. I can't say.   #funny
? week1:true weekday:fri
- Here. Your mug. Your name on it and everything. Welcome to Works, properly.   #warm
- Every new hand gets a mug on their first Friday. It's the law. Well, it's me.   #funny
- Hook's the one on the end of the rack. Yours from now on. Nobody else touches it.
? flag:mug
- Your mug's still on the rack. I gave it a rinse. Don't tell anyone I'm soft.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue)
// He never says no (his thread): his declines are yeses postponed.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- {hi}. Afternoon slump. I've a joke for it. No? Fair. Have you eaten, at least?
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {hi}, stranger. Have you been eating? You've been somewhere. Sit. Tell me.

== near
? place:teacorner
- Kettle's on, mugs on the rack, rota on the wall. All's right with the world.
? habit:garden-lover
- The tomatoes are coming on. I check them every day. They don't seem to mind.
? habit:music
- Music room most evenings now. I sit at the back and tap my foot. Badly.   #funny

== invite
? tier>=acquaintance
- Works tea, one o'clock, tea corner. Bring yourself. I'll find you a mug.
- Come and see the tomatoes after shift? The garden's lovely in the evening.

== accept
- Lovely. Yes. I'll bring something baked. I'll bring two somethings.   #funny
- Yes. I was going to say yes before you finished asking.   #funny

== decline
- I'd love to. I can't. I've said yes to three people tonight. Tomorrow? Please?
- Not tonight, I'm covering the rota. I'm always covering the rota. Next time.

== missed
- I kept you a scone. It's a bit sad now. I'll eat it. For you.   #funny

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday! I baked. I told Brennan it was an emergency. It was.   #funny
? birthday:me
- My birthday. I baked my own cake. Is that sad? It's a very good cake.   #funny

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Saw your job on the board. Done, signed, closed. Lovely. Have a biscuit.   #warm

// ---- Writer 2, batch 1b: a hint (a moment is ready) and an about line for a named friend
== hint
- Could I borrow you a minute later? Not for a job. For me, for once.

== about
? aff:yoon-elif:friend
- Yoon's breakfast jokes are nearly as bad as mine. Nearly. I'm very proud of her.   #funny

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- I've a joke. Nobody wants it. Here it is.   #funny
- Brennan says I can have an oven Saturday.
- Has everyone eaten? Somebody hasn't.
- Tomatoes are nearly red. Nearly.
? act:work
- Kettle's on. Rota's done. Lovely.
?

== rumour
- Lovely bit of news, this.
- Heard it over a scone. Very reliable.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 11: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Lovely. Have you eaten? I've eaten. Mostly biscuits.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm off soon! Have you eaten? Go and eat. That's my goodbye.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- Your first mug, Friday tea. I still think about that. Lovely day. Keep the hook.   #warm

== letter
- Why did the engineer leave the ship? To see if it would miss him. It's a work in progress. Have you eaten?
? tier>=friend
- Baked for the new crew. They didn't have an inspection. I inspected it myself, in Brennan's voice. It passed. Just.

// Writer 5, batch 9: week-1 beats for the onboarding hook (onboarding seat 1's list, 2026-10-17). One flag key per
// line, beat.<beatId>.<n>, said in order as bubbles while you are in the beat's room in its window; best first
// (onboarding drops the rest when you leave). Mail texts: mail.<beatId>, one line "Subject | body", unsigned.

== week1
// mail d5-mug: Friday, if you missed Works tea
? flag:mail.d5-mug
- Your mug | Missed you at tea. Your mug's on the end hook. It's the law. Well, it's me.

// ---- Pillar 5 (head writer, seat W): Emeka teaching the scanner and the first head-scratcher on Day 5 (the main
// version; seat C's flags train.<id>.lead|follow.<step>; lead.take when he leads you to it, lead.done when he hands
// over). Kind 'work'. Every line under a flag plays in order. Bubbles, 60 or fewer.
== work
? flag:train.m7.lead.take
- Follow me. It's a short walk. I'll tell you a joke on the way.   #funny
? flag:train.m7.lead.hold
- Watch. Panel, scanner, and a moment's patience.
- That one's at twenty. There's our culprit.
- The rest read good. Leave them be.
? flag:train.m7.lead.done
- Lovely. Your turn next. I'll be right behind you.
? flag:train.m7.follow.take
- All yours. I'm only here for the company.
? flag:train.m7.follow.hold
- Look first, then scan. Which bar's the lowest?
? flag:train.m7.follow.fetch
- Right shelf. Well done, you.
? flag:train.m7.follow.done
- Right part, first time. Zeke will be thrilled.   #warm
? flag:train.p3.follow.hold
- There's the other note, on the panel. What does it say?
- Swapped the drain valve. Still leaks. So that's two off.
? flag:train.p3.follow.fetch
- Pump. Plumbing shelf. Off you pop.
? flag:train.p3.follow.done
- Floor's dry! Right first time. Zeke will be sorry he missed it.   #warm
? flag:train.p3.hint.2
- Have you read every note? One's not on the card.
? flag:train.p3.hint.3
- Pop over to the washer's panel. There's a note waiting.

// ---- Pillar 5 Step 3 (head writer W2): team jobs (M2), tracing (M3), P1 (H2). Kind 'work', flags as in
// content/works/keys-p5.md "Step 3". Kind, a little fussy, "lovely".
== work
? flag:team.call.start
- Spots, everyone. On my call. Lovely.
? flag:team.call.brace
- Brace. Feet wide. There.
? flag:team.call.pass
- Pass it here, please. Both hands.
? flag:team.call.hold
- Hold it. Nearly. Nearly.
? flag:team.call.crank
- Crank away. Slow and steady.
? flag:team.call.tip
- Tip it. Gently. Hold.
? flag:team.call.valves
- The valves. One, two, three.
? flag:team.call.open
- Open them again. Same order.
? flag:team.call.drain
- Drain it down. The bucket's there.
? flag:team.call.done
- And seated. Lovely work, everyone.   #warm
? flag:train.m9.follow.give
- Clip it on the panel. Gently. Then read.
? flag:train.m9.follow.read
- Full here. So it's further down. Onward.
? flag:train.m9.follow.wrong
- That's upstream. We know it's fine. Back we go.
? flag:train.m9.follow.found
- Full before, low after. There it is. Lovely.
? flag:train.m9.follow.done
- Showers on Four run full. That's tracing, that is.
? flag:train.p1.word
- Here's a puzzle the pipe kit can't solve.
- It only happens sometimes. When? That's the clue.

== promoted
- Lovely. Lovely! Well done, you.   #warm

// ---- Pillar 5 Step 4 (head writer W2): M17 the lift roof (E3), his words on the first ride. Kind 'work', in order.
== work
? flag:roof.climb
- Up you get. Harness clipped? Lovely.
? flag:roof.grease
- Rail, then grease, then a wipe. Next deck.
- Mind your sleeve. The rails love sleeves.   #funny
? flag:roof.view
- Look up. That's the whole spine. Nobody sees it but us.   #warm
? flag:roof.done
- Smoother already. Can you feel it? Lovely work.
